<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/027U">Example <span data-tag="027U">11.5.0.116</span>.</a> Let $\mathscr {F}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{Set})$ be a morphism of simplicial sets, and let $\int _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \mathscr {F}$ be the simplicial set given by Definition <a data-tag="026J" href="/tag/026J">5.6.2.1</a>, so that the projection map $\int _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \mathscr {F} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is a left covering map (see Example <a data-tag="026R" href="/tag/026R">5.6.2.8</a>). Then the covariant transport representation $\operatorname{Tr}_{ \int _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \mathscr {F} / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ is canonically isomorphic to the functor $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\mathscr {F}}: \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \rightarrow \operatorname{Set}$ induced by $\mathscr {F}$. </p>
